s downfall without the  decisive blow he won't be weak enough to  be sealed away or maybe even killed  outright with the sword in this  miserable state yet still remaining in  link's possession i think it's safe to  assume that breathtak ii's story will  focus heavily on finding a way to  reverse the damage done to it the  question is how how do you fix well this  well that's what i want to explore today  we'll take a look at the different  aspects that created the master sword  see if these elements are still  accessible in some way in the era of  breath of the wild and how these could  shape the overall story and gameplay of  the highly anticipated sequel at the end  i'll even throw in some alternative  ideas not because i believe that these  will come to fruition quite the opposite  in fact but more as a way to cover as  much ground as possible i guess so let's  take a look at the possibilities to  restore the master sword  [Music]  [Music]  no matter how iconic or legendary at the  end of the day swords are objects and  thus they can be broken however this  doesn't always have to be the end of it  sometimes it can be remade  it has been remade  it can be restored to its former self or  even forged into something new perhaps  something even better but how do you fix  a sword that has no pieces left to put  back together the master sword isn't  just broken or shattered it's been  melted charred eaten away down to its  very core we've seen that given enough  time and under the right circumstances  the sword can magically regenerate  itself just like it did in the 100 years  following the calamity but with almost  half of the blade completely gone this  might be beyond something time can fix  and even if it could the current  predicaments don't exactly give our  heroes a lot of time to spare all things  considered the damage to the master  sword in breath the wild was pretty  surface level and even then it took  close to a century to heal imagine how  long it would 