ysics second is goddess hylia  who is said to have created the sword  that would serve as the basis for the  master sword as well as giving life to  phi the spirit who dwells within it  we'll get into fire and demise in a  later section after dousing the sword in  the sacred flames it already became  known as the master sword but in order  to defeat demise it needed one final  push after zelda completes her  transformation into the mortal  incarnation of hylia her final blessing  created the true master sword as we know  it and with it the ability to slay even  the most powerful demons who oppose the  gods lastly we have those who awaken as  sages to serve the gods in times of  hardship we've already witnessed  firsthand how sages can uphold or  restore the sword's power when needed  and historically they've also been known  to pass it down protect it or utilize it  in some way such as when the light sage  rauru repurposed it to serve as a key to  the sacred realm it's even possible that  the sages were directly involved in the  creation of the master sword in some way  something zelda implies in twilight  princess stating that the sword was  created by the wisdom of the ancient  sages of course this does go against the  story of skyward's sword after all zelda  clearly states that hylia created the  goddess sword and was subsequently  forged into the master sword by link and  phi no sage was ever involved in this  process however we do find the insignia  of the six ancient sages inside the  temple of hailia which was built long  before skyloft even existed likely  around the time the war with demise and  his army started so i guess it's  possible that when phi says that hylia  created the goddess sword she simply  means it was crafted by her design but  that the sages are the ones who actually  built it for her the same way the shika  built the gates of time by her design as  well not the best solution perhaps since  there's not a lot of evidence to work  with but 