  symbolize none other than the six sages  notice how there's no representation of  the rito first of all and second the  small rock is referred to as a kokiri as  opposed to a korok a name which the  spirits of the forest haven't gone by  for a very long time this matches  exactly with the sages from ocarina of  time specifically whose races all  correspond to one of the six rocks seen  at the pedestal furthermore we could  make the argument that the three flowers  who are linked to princess zelda  symbolize goddess hylia or maybe the  triangle in the center does seeing as  hylia was once the keeper of the  triforce the deku tree aside from being  a story npc also has a more symbolic  contribution to the story as well the  book states that perhaps by hylia's  design a young cherry tree grew beside  the pedestal of the master sword and  that after an eternity had passed he  eventually became its guardian now the  deku tree has always served as a  guardian of sorts so that's nothing new  but what makes this incarnation of him  different is that this deku tree is a  cherry blossom in japanese culture  cherry blossoms represent the circle of  life and death as well as the concept  that nothing is eternal and must one day  come to an end in the context of the  story this is already a fitting metaphor  for the way the master sword works its  power is something that's borrowed it  does not belong to any one individual  once it served its purpose the hero and  the sword part weighs the hero  eventually dies only for a future  incarnation to take up the sword once  again now cherry blossoms are an  extremely rare occurrence in breath of  the wild's hyrule and it just so happens  that the only other location that  features a cherry blossom tree is on  satori mountain right next to the pond  where satori who is said to be an  ancient sage who died on this mountain  makes his appearance the symbolism  regarding the goddesses and sages  doesn't just stop at the pedestal either  inside the temple of time which  poetically enough once served as the  resting place for the master sword ages  ago we can find a large hylia statue on  the altar in the back surrounded by six  smaller statues then we have the seven  megalithic statues found inside the  gerudo desert massive stoneworks  depicting a group of proud warrior women  gripping a giant sword the inscriptions  on these statues have long since been  translated successfully and spell out  the phrase seven sages which might be a  bit confusing for the newcomers but it's  6 ancient sages plus princess zelda or  if you want to be more technical hylia  additionally our favorite mystery tribe  the zonai also seem to have their own  rendition of the six sages it's a statue  of a boar likely representing ganon  surrounded by six pillars one of the  pillars is toppled over and lies flat on  the ground which is why many believe  that this is depicting the sages from  twilight princess since ganondorf kills  one of the sages in this story as for  the goddesses we have the triforce  symbol in the sanctum the sacred springs  of power wisdom and courage as well as  the three ancient dragons dinro nedra  and farage whose names are all derived  from the golden goddesses as well and of  course hyrule has no shortage of hylia  statues big and small so yes despite the  enormous time gap between breath of the  wild and the older games in the series  many important aspects have survived to  various degrees and the ones i just  listed are still but a fraction but the  question remains if we want to fix the  master sword by repeating a similar  process seen in skyward sword are the  components needed to do this still  accessible in some way or at the very  least a viable substitute i believe so  and in fact it could explain a lot about  the possible direction breath of the  wild 2 is heading towards there's still  a lot of unknowns right now but so far  we've been able to see underground  sections a skyrealm and additionally the  surface of hyrule is being repurposed as  well and i think each of these could be  tied to the various elements needed for  the restoration of the master sword  which to recap is the sacred force  originating from the gods hylia's  blessing and possibly one or more sages  so let's tackle them one by one starting  with the force it's unknown if the  sacred flames still exist in the present  day but if they do the only connection  to them that still persists are the  dragons who in the time of skyward sword  were the protectors of the flames which  is where i believe the sky realm could  come into play we visually see the  dragons disappearing into some sort of  sky portal after which they completely  disappear if the sky is indeed the home  of the dragons it would be the best  place to look for the sacred flames or  something that serves a similar function  next is hylia's blessing which is a bit  of a tricky one as it's not exactly  clear what this so-called blessing  entails when she gives link her blessing  in skyward sword all that really happens  is the hilt unfolds and the blade starts  to glow more brightly but as we can see  in the new footage despite the immense  damage the hilt is still extended so i'm  not sure if the sword even needs to be  blessed again but if it does we have  another problem zelda who carries the  essence of hylia is gone right now we  have no idea what her fate could be this  might be a bit dark but the more i look  into it the more i'm starting to  entertain the possibility that the  yellow orb we see floating in front of  link in the new footage could very well  be zelda's spirit zelda is known to emit  yellow energy not just in breath of the  wild but other games as well and is  implied to be her life force  historically it's also been tied to  light-based weapons as well like the  light arrows which are almost always  obtained through her or she wields the  arrows herself it's kind of hard to  imagine nintendo killing a 17 year old  but then again some of the champions  were pretty young as well as long as you  don't show the gruesome details it's  usually okay not to mention that it  wouldn't be the first time that zelda's  soul became separated from her body in  spirit tracks zelda who by the way is  considerably younger here is technically  dead in a way that isn't to say that  zelda is completely done for again like  in spirit tracks she does turn out okay  in the end and in twilight princess she  sacrifices her life force to save mitna  and here too she somehow manages to come  back again let's also not forget that in  breath of the wild she miraculously  survived being gobbled up and trapped  inside ganon's cocoon for 100 years  without aging a day so yeah i think it's  safe to say that she has some pretty  thick plot armor even if she's quote  unquote dead there's always hope left  for her i'm not sure how it ties into  link's new bracelet but if it's an  artifact that can extract souls or life  force it could explain why zelda's  spirit is inside it either way if  hylia's blessing is needed in some way  to restore the sword we might want to  look into getting her back as well  lastly we have the sages and this is  where i think hyrule's surface and its  underground could be utilized when you  complete the trial of the sword you'll  find seven shika monks surrounding the  master sword on a pedestal in the middle  six of which hold a similar pose to one  of the six sages from ocarina of time  it's not clear if these are the sages of  their time or if they're just imitating  a similar ritual but whatever it is that  they're doing it works and restores the  master sword back to its full potential  not only does it bring back its iconic  glow permanently and boosts its attack  power but it even makes it so that link  himself is now able to hear the voice of  phi resonating from within the sword  the problem is that once link completes  the trial the monks having fulfilled  their purpose pass on to the afterlife  so if the power of the sages is needed  to restore the sword in the sequel then  we'll have to find an alternative either  in the form of new individuals who can  awaken as a sage like an ocarina of time  seeking an audience with their spirits  or perhaps collect something like  materials or artifacts that are linked  to the ancient sages i especially like  the idea of collecting some sort of  elemental material like ore after all  the blade has lost a considerable amount  of its steel which i can imagine has to  be replaced in some way so imagine this  seeing as the pedestal inside korok  forest depicts six different individuals  this could mean that the surface and  hyrule's underground hide ancient  dungeons that are connected to  individual sages azor a dungeon hidden  underwater something related to the  kokiri slash koroks inside a forest  somewhere an ancient gerudo temple maybe  below the arbiter's grounds for example  a rito dungeon either in the sky or in  the snowy mountains something inside  death mountain related to the gorons  which would explain why in the teaser  there's no lava flow anymore and since  the shika have historically been tied to  underground locales something found deep  below the earth would be a good fit for  them and depending on how many sages  will be needed there's always room for  even more something tied to the zonai or  maybe the hylians if we combine this  with the possible trials and obstacles  waiting for us in the skies above the  total dungeon count could be incredible  and with a possible secondary objective  of finding a way to bring back zelda  this game could be absolutely massive  obviously i don't want to overhype the  game too much and risk disappointment  but then again the game has been in  development for close to 6 years now one  of the longest development cycles in  zelda history so i don't think it's a  crime to expect something big still that  doesn't mean my theory is correct and  maybe the story and goals will be vastly  different despite the fact that we're  almost 6 years down the road the amount  of info we have on the game is still  painfully small but i do think that what  we've discussed so far does at least  make sense story wise the little clue  sprinkled throughout the footage as well  as the lore and history from past games  does give us little insights into the  possible story directions especially  when it comes to ganondorf's actions and  motivations they seem to reflect all the  knowledge and experience he's collected  and retained from past failures without  hesitation he swiftly gets rid of the  two most important keys to his defeat  zelda and her ceiling power and the  master sword the second teaser also  hints that something has happened to  korok forest possibly something bad  seeing as the deku tree is missing i  also noticed that this part of the  landscape has an earth or sand texture  which also isn't there in breath the  wild it almost seems as if it's been  uprooted or scorched by some immense  force given what we know about the  forest and the pedestal that lies within  which has the ability to revive the  master sword it would be yet another  brilliant move by ganondorf to swing the  odds in his favor  with all that said let's finally talk  briefly about phi and demise two  entities who also share a close  connection to the master sword so close  in fact that they literally exist inside  it contrary to what some may believe i  don't think that fight or demise are  crucial to the master sword's ability to  vanquish evil especially in the case of  demise since the sword was already able  to slay demons before he got sealed  inside it in fact it's the whole reason  why the sword was made in the first  place to kill him the actual power to  seal darkness likely stems entirely from  the gods as for phi well skyward sword  makes it pretty clear that she was  created with the purpose of offering  guidance to the chosen hero to assist  link in carrying out hylia's plan to  forge a weapon capable of defeating  demise once that plan was realized phi  having served her purpose was quite  literally programmed to go into an  everlasting slumber inside the master  sword as such i also don't believe that  her purpose was to subdue demise after  he got sealed inside the sword she  clearly states that her very being her  consciousness is fading away she never  says that she's going in there to keep  demise from breaking free in fact empire  is the one who stands guard for  thousands of years to ensure that this  doesn't happen i know a lot of people  would love to see demise's comeback and  even i wouldn't mind seeing him at least  being referenced in some way but i also  think the part about demise being inside  the master sword is a bit misunderstood  it's not comparable to say ganondorf  being sealed inside the sacred realm or  twilight realm only to break free again  someday demise was killed both in body  and in spirit all that's left of him are  his remains which according to impa have  already started to decay moments after  his defeat that was many many ages ago  so it's hard to believe that anything  physical remains of him at all at this  point and it doesn't have to demise's  legacy is far worse and far more  effective than that his curse is what  set into motion the endless rebirth of  demons born from his hatred one could  even make the argument that in a way  ganondorf himself is an extension of  demise that isn't to say that phi's  existence within the sword serves no  future purpose at all after all she does  say may we meet again in another life  and in breath of the wild we saw the  first signs that fai's consciousness is  reawakening yet again offering guidance  this time to zelda in an attempt to save  the hero's life so who knows maybe she  will have an even bigger role to play in  the sequel we do see a faint blue glow  on the hilt right before link pulls the  sword from its sheet so i'm willing to  believe that she's still in there and as  far as seeking out the means to fix the  sword phi would be the one being who  would know how after all she was heavily  involved in its creation it would be  amazing if we catch a glimpse of her  again especially since traditionally old  companions never make a comeback in  zelda games  let's conclude the video with some  alternatives to today's theory options  which i haven't mentioned so far because  they made less sense to me than my main  theory or i found them to be a bit too  far-fetched the first is time travel  obviously if time travel does exist in  breath of the wild too it would probably  be the easiest way to fix things going  back to before ganondorf destroys the  sword traveling to the age of skyward  sword and reforging it in the sacred  flames there or heck just go to age of  calamity's timeline and bring back that  version of the master sword the problem  i have with this is that i simply don't  see enough evidence of time travel in  the sequel just yet something i'll make  a future video on i also think that  after skyward sword hd and age of  calamity's time travel plot it would be  best not to repeat the same thing again  not every zelda game has to have time  travel to create an interesting  narrative next is the triforce which  wasn't present in breath the wild well  not really anyway if link can somehow  manage to obtain the full triforce he  would be able to wish for the master  sword's revival but i think it goes  without saying that this would be a bit  of a weird way to go about the narrative  i mean if link would have the full  triforce he wouldn't need the master  sword anymore now would he you could  simply wish for ganondorf's obliteration  and that's that it also doesn't really  match with the current setup why  emphasize the broken master sword like  this if we're not gonna use it to fight  ganondorf in some way could he at least  obtain the triforce of courage yeah sure  but that doesn't change the fact that  the master sword is busted the triforce  of courage is not enough to defeat  ganondorf maybe earning the triforce of  courage will be a secondary objective in  the story like in the wind waker but i  don't see link wielding the full  triforce unless he does it after he's  already killed ganondorf maybe as a way  to undo the damage he's done to hyrule  and its people similar to a link to the  past lastly we have the by far most  awesome scenario but also the most  far-fetched and that is that link needs  to go in search of the four sword i mean  ganondorf has been defeated by the four  sword once before it's one of only a few  blades in the zelda universe that can  somewhat match the properties of the  master sword i don't see a whole lot of  evidence that suggests that this will be  the case say for maybe the eye symbol on  link's new shield which does have a  pretty strong resemblance to vati but  that's about it you know what would be  cool if we had to fuse the four sword  and the master sword together creating  the master iv sword and to compensate  ganondorf teams up with vati then in the  final boss fight they do one of those  dragon ball z fusion dances together and  they become vati ganon or vanon but of  course link can now split into four so  he's like and then zelda and mitna show  up and they do a little fusion dance of  their own and become one entity as well  which should have happened in twilight  princess by the way fannin then summons  the moon from a juror's mask and darth  vader and legolas show up and they're  like  alright i think that's enough internet  for today thank you so much for watching  the video be sure to let me know how you  think the story will unfold by leaving a  comment below a big shout out goes to my  hard-working mods on discord to samuel  who created the artwork scene in the  final section of the video and my  patreons and channel members i've got a  few new face